From f3e5571ec9ece209990ca7365d9056d498173ec6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Belkin <anton.belkin@icloud.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:50:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] mac/vulkan: attach Dolby Vision RPUs to the sample buffer
 layer's frames

With --macos-sample-buffer-layer, each frame's RPU is attached to its
CVPixelBuffer, so macOS applies its Dolby Vision display management (the
trims for the display it's on) as QuickTime does: the frame's own, or the
one --macos-dovi-rpu-file gives for its frame number, from a file as
dovi_tool writes RPUs (Annex B, one per frame).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
