     color management. Can be changed while playing.
     ``--vo=gpu-next`` with macOS and Vulkan (macvk) only.
 
+    A Dolby Vision RPU goes along with each frame, for macOS's Dolby Vision display management (the
+    trims for the display it's on, as QuickTime applies them): the one ``--macos-dovi-rpu-file`` gives,
+    or else the frame's own when libplacebo doesn't apply it itself, with
+    ``--vf=format:dolbyvision=no`` (the base layer then plays as it is, e.g. HLG for profile 8.4; set
+    the target to match, e.g. ``--target-trc=hlg --target-prim=bt.2020``).
+
+``--macos-dovi-rpu-file=<file>``
+    Dolby Vision RPUs for ``--macos-sample-buffer-layer`` to attach in place of the frames' own: a
+    file as ``dovi_tool`` writes them (``dovi_tool extract-rpu``, ``dovi_tool generate``: Annex B, one
+    RPU per frame). Frame N of the file goes with the frame at N / fps seconds (``--rebase-start-time``
+    counts from the first), the last one with every frame after it; a file with one RPU applies to all.
+    Can be changed while playing.
